ed the idea of the lack of  prosecution or investigation of the  crimes of this administration and the  lack of prosecution of the crimes of  these private forces I think they all  ultimately stem from the fact that both  of these parties adhere to the same  basic rules of the game and I think I  think that's one of the shameful things  about the political system in this  country interesting that this is coming  up so much now you know I think in some  ways it's you know it's the the euphoria  of the election is wearing off and we're  starting to realize that you know that  yeah they lost the election but they won  a lot and they're gonna get away with it  and there's something really terrifying  and terrible about watching people get  away with crimes on this scale and we're  really we're really feeling the  compromises because they even got away  with it in the campaign itself I mean  this is part of the winning strategy of  not running such a safe campaign you  know how did Obama win this this  election well one of the ways he won was  by giving in on so many important issues  that he never gave the Republicans  anything that they could really sink  their teeth into and that's why they  ended up with you know with Bill Ayers  because he caved on FISA they would have  had a field day with FISA billers was  against it and you know even something  like offshore oil-drilling  you know as soon as it was clear that  that was gonna be a real difference  Obama gave in he said he could see  certain circumstances where that would  be a good idea just like he gave you  know he and he gave retroactive immunity  to the telecoms you know that's another  that that's another example of just  people getting away with these crimes I  was thinking you know the most important  symbolic victory after the elections  will be if Guantanamo is closed right  and I was and that will be that will be  that will be a very very important day  if that happens but this issue of  criminality is y